detector_raw:
{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this packing plan — are you trying to minimize the number of containers used, maximize the total weight (or units) of goods shipped, or something else?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, presenting mutually exclusive options for one decision."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Should the model instead maximize the amount of goods shipped (by weight or by units) subject to the container rules, or is there a different reading of \"all the goods\" you intended?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response presents a single clarification request asking the user to choose between maximizing shipped goods or providing a different interpretation of the goal."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The rule says a container with any type A must also contain at least one type C — is this one-way only (A forces C, but C can appear without A), or should it be two-way (A and C must always appear together in the same containers)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the directionality of the constraint between type A and type C."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since not all goods can be packed, should the model maximize the total weight of goods shipped, or maximize the total number of units shipped?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice between two mutually exclusive objective functions."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "If some goods are left unshipped, is that acceptable (i.e., the available quantities are upper bounds and leftover goods are simply not loaded), or must every unit of every type be shipped?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy decision regarding whether unshipped goods are permitted or if all units must be shipped."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the goods units indivisible (each type must be loaded in whole units per container), or can they be treated as continuous amounts?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the granularity of the goods units (discrete vs. continuous), which constitutes one independent decision point."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say \"use as few containers as possible,\" should the model minimize the number of containers used, or is the number of containers fixed in advance and you just need to decide how to load them?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding whether the container count is a variable to minimize or a fixed constraint, which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since the objective is to minimize the number of containers, and leftover goods are simply not loaded, does the model need to ship at least some minimum amount of goods, or is it acceptable for the model to use zero containers and ship nothing?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a policy choice regarding minimum shipment requirements."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is the 18-ton minimum a hard constraint that applies to any opened container, or is it a target that applies only when the container is fully committed?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding the nature of the 18-ton minimum (hard constraint vs. target), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
